// NAC AI HVAC DESIGNER — manufacturer technical data.
//
// Source: MM Electrical "NEW STOCK UPDATE — TECH DATA SHEETS" workbook supplied
// by NAC, one sheet per brand. These are the manufacturers' own published
// figures, transcribed — NOT anything this application worked out. A field the
// sheet did not state is null, and the engines treat null as "specification
// data required" rather than filling it in.
//
// The field that earns its keep is `returnSpigots`. A ducted fan coil has a
// fixed return connection — one 400 mm spigot, or two at 350 or 400 — and that
// IS the return duct arrangement, decided by the manufacturer, not something to
// derive from a velocity calculation. Where the sheet gives a rectangular
// flange instead, `returnFlangeMm` carries it and the duct is sized the usual
// way back to that flange.
//
// Each brand's sheet carries several sections with different column orders, so
// every row was validated before being written here: airflow has to sit in the
// 30–110 L/s per kW band a ducted fan coil actually runs at, and static
// pressure in 50–350 Pa. 83 rows failed and were DROPPED rather than corrected
// — no specification is a state the engines already handle; a wrong one is not.
// The Samsung DUCTED range failed in full because that sheet's capacity column
// is the minimum, not the nominal — so there are no Samsung ducted specs here
// by design, though its wall splits parsed cleanly and remain.
//
// Regenerate from a reissued workbook rather than editing by hand.

